      en: ["922: First documented mention of the town of Quedlinburg.", "1321: Construction year of the oldest surviving half-timbered house in the town.", "936: Death of King Henry I, whose tomb is located in the collegiate church.", "1994: Inscription of the old town and Castle Hill as a UNESCO World Heritage site.", "80 hectares: The area of the protected town center containing over 1,300 houses.", "936-1802: Period during which the Quedlinburg Abbey existed as an imperial institution."],
